cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dirconn, please cite the version you used."
title: "dirconn: directed functional connectivity for neurophysiology signals"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Hanwei
    email: Liu_H@ukw.de
    affiliation: University Hospital of Wuerzburg
repository-code: "https://github.com/HanweiLiu-Viola/dirconn"
url: "https://hanweiliu-viola.github.io/dirconn/"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - EEG
  - MEG
  - LFP
  - directed connectivity
  - Granger causality
abstract: >-
  dirconn estimates predictive directed functional connectivity (Granger causality, DTF, PDC and
  renormalised PDC, controls for zero-delay mixing, multitaper Granger causality, PCMCI, transfer
  entropy, time-varying measures) from EEG, MEG, iEEG and LFP at sensor and region level. Every
  result carries its provenance and an assumption checklist, and every method is validated on
  simulated networks with a known truth, including simulations through realistic head models.
